# UI design specification

FRAMEWORK: Streamlit

PAGES:
- Starter: build a starterfile.pseudo section by section, then run the pipeline.
- Editor: create or edit pseudocode files and convert them to code.
- Converter: convert pseudocode to code (pseudo2code) and long notes to pseudocode (longtext2pseudo).
- Patcher: a context-aware chat that reads project files and proposes patches.

WORKFLOWS:
Starter starts with a mode choice: **Create new** (enter a project root, then
optionally "Scan root -> REPOMAP" to auto-fill the directory tree from the
folder layout, then "Create starterfile" writes a fresh file) or **Load
existing** (read an on-disk starterfile into the editor). The REPOMAP is edited
as a tree (add/rename/delete directories), not as raw text.
Starter has four tabs. Tab 1 edits # PATHS and # REPOMAP, tab 2 edits
# DATABASES, tab 3 edits # PSEUDOCODE, tab 4 reviews the assembled file and
runs the code_starter pipeline. Tabs 1-3 are edited with structured widgets:
REPOMAP as a tree (add/rename/delete directories); the Databases tab as a
builder (add databases -> tables -> columns with add/remove controls, where
every table needs an identifier column); the Pseudocode tab as one card per
script module -- a path chosen from the REPOMAP folders, the preset fields
(INPUT, OUTPUT, TASK, CONDITIONS, PREFERENCES) and an optional FUNCTION MODEL
(steps, math formulas, criteria). Each of tabs 1-3 has a Verify button; on
success a write button appears (tab 2's reads "Append DATABASES to
starterfile", tab 3's "Append PSEUDOCODE to starterfile") and the section is
written into the starterfile. PSEUDOCODE verification also cross-checks every
module path against the REPOMAP folders (the structure-orphan-file rule). Once
a section is appended, later edits and removals rewrite that section on disk.
Tab 4 auto-assembles the sections (no manual reassembly) and shows the whole
file as coloured, read-only HTML with summary counters; it can write/verify the
file and then runs the pipeline in the background, showing a per-stage report.

INPUTS AND OUTPUTS:
Project root and starterfile name are inputs. Section editors are multi-line
text areas and a tree widget; files are also rewritten directly on disk by
Create and Save. Verification failures are shown as errors; successes as
messages. The pipeline report shows each stage pass/fail plus the smoke-test
artifact.

VISUAL DESIGN:
A left sidebar lists the four pages. Wide layout, one primary column, tabs for
sub-sections, status messages inline.

ACCESSIBILITY:
Labels on every input, keyboard-navigable tabs, sufficient contrast.
